.\" Manual page for box
.TH BOX 1 "2026-11-26" "box 0.14.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
box \- browse local image archives, online boorus and a Hydrus library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B box
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIROOT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B box
(BOoru eXplorer) is a native Qt6 client for online boorus and for local
image archives written by gallery\-dl or similar tools.
It reads per\-file sidecar metadata from local folders, browses Danbooru,
Gelbooru, Moebooru, Szurubooru, Shimmie, HyBooru, Nuuru, Philomena,
Booru\-on\-Rails and e\-shuushuu instances, downloads posts in full quality and keeps
favourites in a local SQLite store. An optional read\-only Box Share web
gallery and Danbooru\-shaped LAN server shares selected local sources with
a browser, LoliSnatcher, another Box instance, or any HTTP client (default
0.0.0.0:7071). A red LIVE badge in the status bar shows while it runs. An
optional Hydrus
tab keeps a
separate local library keyed by SHA\-256 and reads tags from a local
Hydrus/hydd API without writing back.
.PP
Booru instances, storage folders, themes and download behaviour are managed
from the graphical Preferences dialog; settings persist in
.IR settings.ini .
.PP
A fresh profile makes no network requests until the user explicitly opens
a remote tab, searches, downloads or opens Hydrus. Automatic tag
categorization is off by default; Preferences \(-> Taxonomies selects one
explicit backend (off, local Hydrus namespaces, Danbooru, Gelbooru,
Safebooru, Yandere or a custom URL). There is no hidden fallback.
.PP
Only one instance runs at a time. A second copy exits with a message.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-stylesheet \fIfile.qss\fR
Apply a custom Qt stylesheet on top of the selected theme for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-native\-theme
Use the desktop environment's Qt theme instead of the built\-in theme.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a short help summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-all
Include Qt's own command line options in the help output.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I ROOT
Folder to scan on startup. Without it
.B box
opens the last used tab, or the welcome page on first launch.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/box/settings.ini
User settings (booru list, theme, storage folders, UI state).
.TP
.I ~/.config/box/themes/
Optional theme drop\-ins, one INI file per theme. A file with the same name
as a bundled theme overrides it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/box/
Data folder: favourites store, Hydrus tab database and media folder, tag
category database, cache bookkeeping database, default downloads and the
rotating
.IR box.log .
.TP
.I ~/.cache/box/
Thumbnail and media caches.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BOX_CONFIG_DIR
Use this folder instead of
.I ~/.config/box
for settings and theme drop\-ins.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME
Standard XDG base directories used when
.B BOX_CONFIG_DIR
is unset and no custom storage folders were configured in the app.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal termination.
.TP
.B 1
Startup failure (for example another instance is already running, or a
configured storage folder is unavailable).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gallery\-dl (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.PP
Project home: https://github.com/lusoterra/box
